This is a draft description on how to use the NDN version of murmur.

1. Go to the follow link to download the mumble client:
http://mumble.sourceforge.net/

2. Launch the ccnd and connect to the ccn hub near you.

3. Set your local prefix by setting the LOCAL_PREFIX environment variable.
E.g. export LOCAL_PREFIX="/ucla.edu/cs/zhenkai/"
Note that local prefix MUST end with a slash ("/"). We will make the code smart in next release.

4. Launch the murmurd in ./debug directory. If you are using prebuild binary, run murmurd.sh instead.

5. Launch the Mumble client and start chatting! You can use any username you want when asked for.

Footnote: current version of ndn murmur assumes that there is only one channel: root. That is, everyone
using ndn murmur will appear in root.


